## 1. FIX THE CURRENT FAILURE BEFORE ADDING MORE FEATURES

The current application sometimes takes too long to think, fails to provide an answer promptly, and has produced long document-generation instructions in response to ordinary messages.

Perform a real technical audit.

Inspect the complete request lifecycle:

- User message submission.
- Prompt construction.
- Conversation history.
- Model selection.
- Provider API requests.
- Tool execution.
- Model routing.
- Response streaming.
- Response parsing.
- Frontend state updates.
- Errors, retries and cancellation.
- Task-specific prompts.
- Any background operations.

Identify the actual causes of excessive latency, empty responses, duplicated calls, stuck generation and irrelevant answers.

Do not hide bugs behind a loading animation. Fix them at the source.

### Mandatory behaviour

When a user asks a straightforward question, return a straightforward answer.

When the user asks a complex technical question, use the appropriate level of analysis.

When the user sends an incomplete message, ask a brief clarification.

When a user requests a PDF, invoke the document workflow.

When a user asks to build an application, invoke the coding workspace.

Do not let specialised prompts leak into general chat. Do not inject a document-generation template into ordinary conversation.

Never require the user to wait indefinitely for an answer.

If a provider fails, times out or produces an empty response, handle the error properly and offer an appropriate retry or fallback. Do not automatically repeat expensive requests without limits.

A model failure must not become an infinite loading indicator.

