## 5. INTEGRATE NVIDIA TECHNOLOGY WHERE IT ACTUALLY HELPS

Investigate suitable official NVIDIA tools and repositories.

Potential integrations include:

### NVIDIA NIM

Official documentation:

https://docs.nvidia.com/nim/

NVIDIA NIM can provide model-inference services through supported APIs and deployments. Check the actual available models, API format, authentication requirements, usage terms and deployment options.

Use a hosted endpoint when it fits the existing environment and is properly configured.

If using a hosted NVIDIA inference API, integrate it through a secure server-side provider adapter.

Do not claim that NIM has been installed locally when the application is actually calling a hosted endpoint.

### NVIDIA TensorRT-LLM

Official repository:

https://github.com/NVIDIA/TensorRT-LLM

Evaluate TensorRT-LLM for optimised model inference when suitable NVIDIA GPU infrastructure is available.

Inspect its compatibility with the selected model, CUDA environment, dependencies and deployment platform before integrating it.

Use it for the inference workload it is designed to accelerate. Do not install GPU-specific infrastructure into an incompatible browser-only environment.

### NVIDIA NeMo

Official repository:

https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo

Evaluate suitable NeMo components for model training, fine-tuning, evaluation or related workflows when the project's goals and infrastructure justify them.

Do not treat model-training infrastructure as an automatic improvement to the answers of a running third-party API model.

### NVIDIA GPU and cloud execution

Detect the actual environment.

If supported NVIDIA GPU compute is available, select compatible optimisation strategies.

If not, use a properly configured remote inference service or another available backend.

Do not claim to possess an NVIDIA GPU, additional VRAM, CUDA acceleration or unlimited processing power without verifying that the capability exists.

Do not force the user's ordinary laptop to run an impractical large model locally.

### NVIDIA integration acceptance criteria

For each integration, verify:

- Official repository or documentation.
- License and applicable service terms.
- Model and runtime compatibility.
- Hardware requirements.
- API or deployment configuration.
- Security requirements.
- Actual successful inference.
- Measurable effect on latency or throughput.

If an integration does not fit the application, document why and choose an appropriate alternative.

