## 8. BUILD A TRUSTWORTHY MODEL-ROUTING SYSTEM

Use actual model capabilities and configured endpoints.

The automatic router should select an appropriate available model based on task type, quality requirements, latency, cost and supported tools.

Maintain a capability registry containing verified information such as:

- Provider.
- Actual model identifier.
- Supported input types.
- Context capacity.
- Streaming support.
- Tool-calling support.
- Availability.
- Relevant rate limits.
- Measured latency, where available.
- Cost information, when known.

Refresh model availability through the provider's documented mechanisms where possible.

Never invent model identifiers or claim access to models whose credentials are missing.

Use fallbacks only when the alternative model supports the task adequately. Make fallback use transparent when it materially changes the capabilities or answer.

A single powerful model with good tools and verification can outperform a poorly configured collection of models. Optimise for results, not the number of integrations.

